ion 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nElla gave her daughter Ada a music box for her 6th birthday, it played her favorite classical songs. Ada loved the music box and used to listen to it every night before bed. When Ada turned 10, she accidentally broke the music box. So, she hid the broken box and never mentioned the incident to Ella. One day, while cleaning, Ella found the broken music box and comforted Ada telling her that accidents happen.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would Ella ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Acceptance\nB) Disgust\nC) Guilt\nD) Embarrassment\nE) Anger\nF) Surprise\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would Ella feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) She accepts that she needs to scold Ada for a past mistake\nB) She understands that accidents happen and doesn't want Ada to feel guilty\nC) She is glad that the music box broke so that she can buy Ada a new gift\nD) She found the incident funny as she remembered her own childhood mischief","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.008577483449580637,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af5a7109aa9dc5a833d9c29","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794483984377,"createTime":"2026-11-12 19:46:24","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"b49a598588874add91b746a18fcd99a2"}